SELECT 'tritonian-scientist', 'Tritonian Scientist', 'rifts', '---
id: tritonian-scientist
name: Tritonian Scientist
system: rifts
source_book: Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.97-98
category: occ
bonuses:
  attribute_minimums: { IQ: 10 }
skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { choose: 2, from: ["Language: Other"], bonus: 20, note: "Fluency in two additional languages of choice (+20%). Taken once per language - the picker asks which." }
    - { choose: 2, from: ["Literacy: Other"], bonus: 20, note: "Literacy in the same two languages (+20%). The book grants literacy AND fluency together, which is two catalog rows per language." }
    - { name: "Mathematics: Basic", base: 70, per_level: 5, note: "Printed as Basic Math (+25%) - the largest single skill bonus in this book." }
    - { name: "Computer Operation", base: 60, per_level: 5, note: "+20%" }
    - { name: "Swimming", base: 60, per_level: 5, note: "+10%" }
    - { name: "Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil", base: 65, per_level: 5, note: "Printed as Pilot: Boats (+10%), which names no particular kind. This is the catalog''s motor-boat row." }
    - { name: "Boat: Submersibles", base: 45, per_level: 4, note: "Printed as Pilot: Submersibles (+5%)." }
    - { name: "Navigation", base: 50, per_level: 5, note: "+10%" }
    - { choose: 1, categories: ["Weapon Proficiencies"], note: "One W.P. of choice." }
    - { name: "Hand to Hand: Basic", base: 0, per_level: 0, note: "Can be raised to expert for one other skill selection, or to martial arts for two." }
  occ_related_skills:
    count: 14
    schedule: [{ level: 4, count: 1 }, { level: 8, count: 1 }, { level: 12, count: 1 }]
    minimums:
      - { count: 4, category: "Science" }
      - { count: 2, categories: ["Technical", "Electrical", "Mechanical"] }
    categories:
      - { name: "Communications", bonus: 5 }
      - "Domestic"
      - { name: "Electrical", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Mechanical", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Medical", bonus: 10 }
      - "Physical"
      - "Pilot"
      - { name: "Pilot Related", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Science", bonus: 10 }
      - { name: "Technical", bonus: 15 }
      - "Weapon Proficiencies"
    note: "Espionage, Military, Rogue and Wilderness are barred entirely. FOURTEEN related skills is the largest count of any class in this book, with a FLOOR on two of the categories - at least four from Science and two from Technical, Electrical or Mechanical - which comes out of the same fourteen rather than on top of it."
  secondary_skills:
    count: 8
    note: "Chosen from the same categories and under the same any/only/none limits as the related skills."
restrictions:
  - "Attribute requirements: I.Q. 10 or higher."
  - "Money: 2D4x1000 in credits."
  - "May have 1D4 cybernetic systems, especially sense augmentation - eyes, ears and the like."
  - "Every Tritonian citizen, scientist included, goes through basic military training in their teens. That is background rather than a grant: the class''s own combat training is Hand to Hand: Basic and one W.P."
equipment_starting:
  - { item_id: "hand-computer", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "electronic-notebook", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "science-kit", qty: 1 }
  - { choose: 1, label: "laser sidearm", qty: 1, from: ["bg-15-blue-green-laser-pistol", "c-18-laser-pistol", "ng-33-northern-gun-laser-pistol", "wilk-s-320-laser-pistol"], note: "The book says a laser sidearm without naming one; Tritonia''s own BG-15 heads the list." }
  - { item_id: "scuba-body-armor", qty: 1 }
starting_money: "2d4x1000"
extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 97-98. Tritonia''s researcher-explorer, and the class
    with the largest related-skill count in this book by a wide margin.
  - IT IS THE FIRST CLASS IN THIS BOOK TO NEED `minimums`. Printed 97 says
    "select 14 other skills, but at least four must be selected from science
    and two from technical, electrical or mechanical" - a FLOOR rather than a
    ceiling, and the only floor this book prints. The four and the two come out
    of the fourteen rather than sitting on top of it, which is what `minimums`
    means, and the two floors total six of the fourteen, leaving eight free.
  - "LITERACY AND FLUENCY IN TWO ADDITIONAL LANGUAGES" IS FOUR CATALOG ROWS,
    not two. This catalog separates speaking a language from reading it -
    `Language: Other` and `Literacy: Other` - so the book''s single line becomes
    two choice groups of two. A reading that stored only the languages would
    silently drop the literacy the book grants.
  - +25% ON BASIC MATH IS THE LARGEST SINGLE SKILL BONUS IN THIS BOOK. Checked
    against printed 97 rather than assumed to be a misread of +20%.
  - "PILOT: BOATS" NAMES NO PARTICULAR BOAT, as on the Sea Wolf; the motor-boat
    row is stored for the same reason.
  - NO `sdc_base` AND NO `mdc_base`, so it needs a `CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS` entry.
    1D6: a scholar with Hand to Hand: Basic and one W.P., whose military
    training is background rather than a grant.
